  "worked_solution": "The cardinality of a finite set $A$ is the number of elements in $A.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $A:$\n\n$$\n4,\\,{6,11},\\,5,\\,{7,13,15},\\,{8,2}\n$$\n\nNote that ${6,11}$,  ${7,13,15}$ and ${8,2}$ each count as single elements of $A.$\n\nSince $A$ has $5$ elements, the cardinality is $|A|=5.$",
